\p{\strong{8:27 AM}}
\hr
\p{Finished \em{Today's [GEB](hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999)}. LOTs on recursion today. The examples were not exactly illustrative. Although, I guess their complexity ended up being one of the main points of the chapter. Namely, that from somewhat harmless looking recursive equations things can quickly start to expand into unintelligible complexity (may this be the key to intelligence???). The book did show its age when talking about chess. Particularly, that humans were still substantially better than machines...}
